# UAV Ground Control Station

Use these rules when working in this repository.

## Scope

- Keep the project a slim local GCS for UAVs.
- Treat the desktop Tauri app as the canonical operator runtime.
- Keep the browser + Node path as the dev/fallback runtime.
- Avoid adding mission planning, parameter editing, fleet management, or reports unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture

- Use TypeScript throughout the monorepo.
- Keep shared contracts in `packages/shared`.
- Keep production TX16S/CRSF/COM hardware access in `apps/desktop` via Tauri/Rust.
- Keep `apps/server` for the browser dev/fallback MAVLink path.
- Keep `apps/web` visualization-only.
- On Windows, prefer desktop over WSL-hosted Node so host `COM*` ports work without USB passthrough.

## Workspace conventions

- Update `README.md` whenever setup, commands, APIs, telemetry behavior, environment variables, architecture, or operator workflow changes.
- Bump the app version for every functional change.
- Keep `package.json`, `apps/desktop/package.json`, `apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`, and `apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml` in sync so MSI upgrades install over older versions.
- On Windows development machines, run normal repo maintenance commands through WSL.
- Exception: native Tauri desktop dev/build should run in a Windows terminal when testing host `COM*` hardware access.

## Hardware and telemetry

- Keep serial-port handling cross-platform for macOS `/dev/cu.*` and `/dev/tty.*`, Windows `COM*`, and Linux `/dev/ttyACM*` / `/dev/ttyUSB*`.
- Preserve manual path entry for unusual USB serial devices.
- Filter out empty system serial ports unless device metadata indicates real attached hardware.
- Prefer USB/PNP-backed ports in the UI.
- Normalize incoming link data into `TelemetryState`.
- Preserve the shared `TelemetryState` shape unless the frontend and README are updated together.
- Keep WebSocket payloads JSON and small enough for local real-time display.
- Maintain the track limit of 5000 points in the frontend unless there is a deliberate performance change.

## UI direction

- Keep the dark technical GCS feel.
- Use MapLibre as the dominant central view.
- Prefer simple local components over adding UI frameworks.
- Avoid unnecessary animation.
- Keep the 1920x1080 layout strong while remaining usable on 13-14 inch laptops.

## Completion bar

- Before marking any functional change as complete, run `& "$env:APPDATA\npm\pnpm.cmd" build:desktop` in PowerShell.
- Treat build warnings as cleanup signals, not noise.
- If the desktop build cannot be run, clearly say why and include the missing build step in the final notes.
- When a change is complete, working, and tested, propose a detailed commit message before finishing.